    "author": "Family Travel Asia Team",
    "content": "---\n\ntitle: \"Best Family Beach Resorts in Thailand for Toddlers and Teens\"\nslug: best-family-beach-resorts-thailand\ndate: 2026-05-14\ndescription: \"The best family beach resorts in Thailand for toddlers and teens in 2026. Phuket, Krabi, Koh Samui and hidden gems with kids clubs, pools and value.\"\ntags: [\"family-travel\", \"thailand\", \"beach-resorts\", \"asia\", \"phuket\", \"krabi\", \"koh-samui\"]\nauthor: \"Family Travel Asia Team\"\ncategory: \"guides\"\nimage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?w=1200\"\n\n# Best Family Beach Resorts in Thailand for Toddlers and Teens\n\nThailand is a top destination for family vacations, offering stunning beaches, delicious cuisine, and rich culture. When it comes to choosing the best family beach resorts in Thailand, there are many options to consider. From luxurious villas to budget-friendly bungalows, we've got you covered.\n\n## Top Resorts in Phuket with Kids Clubs\n\nPhuket is a favorite among families, offering a range of activities and amenities that cater to all ages. Here are some top family beach resorts in Phuket with kids clubs:\n\n*   **Amanpuri**: This luxurious resort offers a kids' club with activities like treasure hunts, beach games, and arts and crafts. The resort also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the Andaman Sea. Prices start from around $500 per night for a family suite.\n*   **Trisara**: Trisara is a luxury resort that offers a kids' club with a focus on outdoor activities like kayaking and paddleboarding. The resort also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $1,000 per night for a family villa.\n*   **Safire Phuket**: Safire Phuket is a beachfront resort that offers a kids' club with activities like beach games and arts and crafts. The resort also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the Andaman Sea. Prices start from around $300 per night for a family suite.\n\n## Krabi Family Resorts for Toddlers\n\nKrabi is another popular destination for families, offering stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. Here are some top family beach resorts in Krabi that cater to toddlers:\n\n*   **Palm Bungalows**: Palm Bungalows is a budget-friendly resort that offers cozy bungalows with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. The resort also features multiple pools, including a kids' pool and an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $200 per night for a family bungalow.\n*   **Krabi Beach Club**: Krabi Beach Club is a beachfront resort that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. The resort also features multiple pools, including a kids' pool and an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $400 per night for a family villa.\n*   **Dusit Thani Laguna Karon**: Dusit Thani Laguna Karon is a luxury resort that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. The resort also features multiple pools, including a kids' pool and an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $800 per night for a family villa.\n\n## Koh Samui Villas for Teens\n\nKoh Samui is a popular destination for families with teens, offering stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. Here are some top villas in Koh Samui that cater to teenagers:\n\n*   **The Siam**: The Siam is a luxury resort that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the surrounding countryside. The resort also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $500 per night for a family villa.\n*   **Villa Seri**: Villa Seri is a luxury villa that offers private access to a secluded beach and crystal-clear waters. The villa also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $1,000 per night for a family villa.\n*   **The Resort at Koh Samui**: The Resort at Koh Samui is a luxury resort that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. The resort also features multiple pools, including an infinity pool with stunning views of the surrounding countryside. Prices start from around $400 per night for a family villa.\n\n## Hidden Gems Like Koh Lanta and Hua Hin\n\nIf you're looking for something off the beaten path, consider visiting Koh Lanta or Hua Hin. Both destinations offer stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters, as well as a range of activities and amenities that cater to families.\n\n*   **Koh Lanta**: Koh Lanta is a tranquil island in southern Thailand that offers stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. The island also features multiple waterfalls, hiking trails, and scenic viewpoints.\n*   **Hua Hin**: Hua Hin is a popular beach town on the mainland that offers stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. The town also features multiple attractions, including a historic railway station and a national monument.\n\n## Budget Options\n\nIf you're looking for budget-friendly options, consider visiting one of these resorts:\n\n*   **Palm Bungalows**: Palm Bungalows is a budget-friendly resort in Krabi that offers cozy bungalows with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. Prices start from around $200 per night for a family bungalow.\n*   **Krabi Beach Club**: Krabi Beach Club is a beachfront resort in Krabi that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. Prices start from around $400 per night for a family villa.\n*   **The Resort at Koh Samui**: The Resort at Koh Samui is a luxury resort in Koh Samui that offers spacious villas with private balconies overlooking the Andaman Sea. Prices start from around $400 per night for a family villa.\n\n## Best Time to Visit\n\nThe best time to visit Thailand depends on your preferences and what you're looking for. Generally, the best time to visit is during the cooler months of November to April, when the weather is pleasant and there are fewer crowds.\n\n## Related Destinations\n\nIf you're looking for other destinations that cater to families, consider visiting one of these places:\n\n*   **Bali**: Bali is a popular destination for families, offering stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. The island also features multiple attractions, including temples, waterfalls, and scenic viewpoints.\n*   **Vietnam**: Vietnam is a popular destination for families, offering stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. The country also features multiple attractions, including ancient ruins, temples, and scenic viewpoints.\n*   **Singapore**: Singapore is a modern city-state that offers stunning architecture and world-class amenities. The city also features multiple attractions, including gardens, museums, and theme parks.\n*   **Malaysia**: Malaysia is a popular destination for families, offering stunning beaches and crystal-clear waters. The country also features multiple attractions, including ancient ruins, temples, and scenic viewpoints.\n\n## The Verdict\n\nThailand is a top destination for family vacations, offering stunning beaches, delicious cuisine, and rich culture. When it comes to choosing the best family beach resorts in Thailand, there are many options to consider. From luxurious villas to budget-friendly bungalows, we've got you covered.\n\nWhether you're looking for a relaxing vacation or an action-packed adventure, Thailand has something for everyone. So why wait? Book your trip today and make some unforgettable memories with your loved ones!\n\n<!-- affiliate:booking.com/beach-resorts-thailand -->\n",
