    "title": "Best Family-Friendly Resorts in Phuket with Kids Clubs (2026)",
    "author": "Captain",
    "content": "# Best Family-Friendly Resorts in Phuket with Kids Clubs (2026)\n\nPhuket is one of Asia's best family beach destinations. We've tested the top resorts with our own kids to find which ones truly deliver for families.\n\n## What Makes a Great Kids Club?\n\n- Supervised hours (at least 6 hours/day, including evenings)\n- Age-appropriate programs for toddlers, kids, and tweens\n- Qualified childcare professionals\n- Indoor-outdoor balance (AC playrooms + outdoor playgrounds)\n- Meals included in some programs\n\n## 1. Club Med Phuket\n\nRating: 5/5\n\nClub Med Phuket is the gold standard for family resorts in Asia.\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Petit Club (2-3 years): Supervised play, arts, music, naps\n- Mini Club (4-10 years): Trapeze, sailing, arts and crafts, sports\n- Passworld (11-17 years): Teens-only activities, social events\n\nWhy it works: Trained G.O.s (Gentle Organizers) keep kids engaged while parents enjoy adult-only spaces. The kids' club runs from 9 AM to 9 PM.\n\nPool: Freeform pool with kids' section and water features.\n\nBest for: Families who want genuine time off while kids have a vacation of their own.\n\nPrice: ~$250-400/night all-inclusive\n\n[Book on Klook](https://www.klook.com/en-US/activity/622-club-med-phuket/)\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=1)\n\n## 2. Anantara Vacation Club Mai Khao\n\nRating: 4.5/5\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Anantara Kidz Club (4-12 years): Thai boxing, fruit carving, Batik painting\n- Supervised from 9 AM to 6 PM\n- Evening babysitting available\n\nUnique Feature: The resort has the longest lagoon pool in Phuket (300m). Kids can swim from their room to the restaurant.\n\nBest for: Extended stays with apartment-style accommodation (full kitchen, separate bedrooms).\n\nPrice: ~$200-350/night for 2-bedroom\n\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-10&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## 3. Holiday Inn Resort Phuket (Patong)\n\nRating: 4.5/5\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Planet Trekkers (4-12 years): Video games, arts, outdoor activities\n- Supervised from 8 AM to 6 PM\n\nUnique Feature: Massive lagoon-style pool complex with waterslides. The kids' pool area has splash pads and fountains.\n\nBest for: Families who want Patong Beach access with a resort bubble.\n\nPrice: ~$100-200/night\n\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## 4. Sunwing Resort Kamala\n\nRating: 4.5/5\n\nThis resort is designed specifically for families with young children. The entire property is kid-focused.\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Sunwing Kids Club (1-12 years): Multiple age groups\n- Water play area and dedicated kids' pool\n- Daily activity schedule with shows, treasure hunts, and pool games\n\nUnique Feature: Kids' water park with small slides, splash pads, and a pirate ship play structure.\n\nBest for: Families with toddlers and preschoolers.\n\nPrice: ~$120-250/night\n\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## 5. JW Marriott Phuket Resort & Spa\n\nRating: 4/5\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Kids Club (4-12 years): Thai cooking, Batik painting, beach games\n- Supervised from 9 AM to 5 PM\n\nUnique Feature: Turtle release program at nearby Mai Khao beach. The resort grounds are massive with multiple pools.\n\nBest for: Families who want a large resort with plenty of space and options.\n\nPrice: ~$150-350/night\n\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## 6. Centara Grand Beach Resort Phuket (Karon)\n\nRating: 4/5\n\nKids Club Programs:\n- Kids Club (4-12 years): Daily activities, games, crafts\n- Teens Club (13-17 years): Gaming, sports, movie nights\n\nUnique Feature: Multiple pool areas including a dedicated kids' pool with water features. Direct beach access to Karon Beach.\n\nBest for: Families who want a variety of dining and activity options.\n\nPrice: ~$130-280/night\n\n[Check rates on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## 7. Kata Beach Resorts (multiple)\n\nKata Beach has several family-friendly resorts including:\n- **Kata Thani** - Large pool, kids' club, direct beach access\n- **Kata Palm Resort** - Multiple pools, family rooms, budget-friendly\n- **Club Med Kata** - All-inclusive with excellent kids' club\n\nBest for: Families who want easy beach and restaurant access in a family-focused area.\n\n## Kids Club Comparison Table\n\n| Resort | Ages | Hours | Evening Care | Pool Quality | Price |\n|--------|------|-------|-------------|-------------|-------|\n| Club Med | 2-17 | 9AM-9PM | Yes | Excellent | $$$ |\n| Anantara Mai Khao | 4-12 | 9AM-6PM | Extra | Excellent (300m pool) | $$$ |\n| Holiday Inn Patong | 4-12 | 8AM-6PM | No | Great (waterslides) | $$ |\n| Sunwing Kamala | 1-12 | Varies | No | Great (water park) | $$ |\n| JW Marriott | 4-12 | 9AM-5PM | Extra | Good | $$$ |\n| Centara Karon | 4-17 | Varies | No | Good | $$ |\n\n## Tips for Choosing a Phuket Family Resort\n\n- Check kids club age limits - some don't accept under 4\n- Look for \"Kids Stay Free\" programs (Holiday Inn, Sunwing)\n- Consider location - Mai Khao is quiet, Patong is busy, Kata is balanced\n- Read recent reviews - kids club quality can change with management\n- Book directly for best family packages with meals included\n\n## The Verdict\n\nClub Med Phuket is our top pick for families who want genuine time off. Sunwing Kamala is perfect for families with toddlers. Holiday Inn Patong offers the best value with waterslides.\n\n[Browse all Phuket family resorts on Booking.com](https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket&checkin=2026-06-01&checkout=2026-06-07&group_adults=2&group_children=2)\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which Phuket resort has the best kids club?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Club Med Phuket has the most comprehensive kids club with age-specific programs from 2-17 and hours from 9 AM to 9 PM. Their trained G.O.s provide exceptional childcare.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the best area in Phuket for families?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Kata and Karon beaches offer calm waters and family-friendly resorts. Mai Khao is quiet and secluded. Patong is busier but has the widest range of dining.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do Phuket kids clubs accept toddlers?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Club Med accepts from age 2, Sunwing Kamala from age 1. Most other resorts start at age 4. Always check the specific age policy before booking.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are there all-inclusive family resorts in Phuket?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, Club Med Phuket is the premier all-inclusive option. Centara Grand also offers all-inclusive packages. Holiday Inn offers breakfast-inclusive rates.\"}}]}\n</script>\n",
